  "verbalization": "Jatamanin C appears to have a shared target relationship with U373 MG through a series of intermediate compounds, all of which are targets of SNU-387. This suggests that Jatamanin C may act through a common mechanism that targets SNU-387, which in turn targets U373 MG. The evidence indicates that Jatamanin C may exert its biological effect by interacting with SNU-387, which is a key player in the pathway leading to U373 MG. The presence of multiple pathways converging on SNU-387 supports the idea that Jatamanin C may act through a shared target, potentially modulating the same molecular process that influences U373 MG. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SNU-387 as a central node in the interaction network between Jatamanin C and U373 MG.",
